# Amy OS v1.0 — Founder Architecture Lock

Amy OS v1.0 is **complete**. Future work must **extend** the system. It must **not** redesign it.

## Forbidden without explicit Founder Architecture Review

Do **not** introduce:

- New engines
- New registries
- New pipelines
- New abstraction layers
- New ownership models

## Allowed extension paths only

All future functionality must be implemented as one of:

1. **Experience Definitions** — register definitions via the frozen Experience Template Engine (`src/v2/experience-template/`) and Experience Packs pattern (`src/v2/experience-packs/`). Prefer definitions over handwritten packs.
2. **Surface Integrations** — bind frozen Brain / Experience outputs into Legacy surfaces (Today, Coach, Ask Amy, For Child) without changing ownership. Surfaces remain Legacy owners of UI unless a Founder Review says otherwise.

## Frozen stack (do not replace)

Treat as frozen infrastructure to **use**, not rewrite:

- Amy Memory → Context → Decision → Stability → History → Cooldown → Attention Budget
- Registry Adapters → Decision Bridge → Shadow Validation
- Today Brain Adapter / Recommendation Adapter / Resolver / Hero Activation Gate
- Experience Resolver → Experience Template Engine → Speech Experience Pack

## Defaults

- Feature flags for Amy OS V2 slices stay **OFF** until an explicit bind sprint.
- No new Brain / Decision logic unless a Founder Architecture Review authorizes it.
- No UI redesign disguised as “architecture cleanup.”

Only an **explicit Founder Architecture Review** may modify this architecture.
